      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "· Design Inspiration ·",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Louis Vuitton's 2026 Cruise womenswear show took \"Theatre\" as its theme. Artistic Director of Women's Collections Nicolas Ghesquière drew on the Gothic architecture of the Palais des Papes, its painted frescoes, and knightly attire, building fresh fashion ideas through sculptural tailoring, dreamlike jacquard prints, and sumptuous details—exploring the performative character and narrative tension of clothing.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "text": "Louis Vuitton 2026 Cruise collection runway (swipe left/right for more images)",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Bags such as the Petite Malle Capitale trunk and the Speedy Trunk 20 take their cue from medieval battle armor, paired with strong, structured silhouettes and hardware—as if donning the armor of Joan of Arc.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
